From 5b766a4121a6ac21feade104577e21eb9d4afa1e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "HT9045 Machine (V906)" <Claude_RDBC_02@honprec.com>
Date: Thu, 1 Oct 2026 19:55:17 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] CLOSE-BUSY: Exit closes when every 1203 axis is servo OFF /
 in alarm with command velocity 0, even if the card reads BUSY and refuses the
 stop
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EastSun 20261001 19:11 "我關軟體的時候 關不了 你要想辦法": after the 16:36:20 power loss (every axis alm, cardErr 0x80005115) all 19
axes went ERROR_STOP -> BUSY (state 11) at 16:39:03 with servo OFF and cmd velocity 0; at Exit the decel stop + ExtDrive 0 drew
38 vendor errors and the read-back stayed BUSY, so Q44 blocked the close -- and [強制關閉] needs golden Exit's level (Operator had
none), so the program could not be closed.
FileRW/MainClose.cpp: new w906q44::AxisUndrivable -- monitor sample valid, command velocity 0, SVON bit off or ALM bit on, state
DISABLE / READY / ERROR_STOP / BUSY -> the card cannot drive it, it counts as stopped; a failed stop on such an axis is "not
needed", not "not sent". Still holds as before: servo ON without alarm, velocity != 0, any motion state (HOMING included, even
at velocity 0), servo reading invalid (ioValid defaults false). Reason text puts the conclusion first (the oplog keeps 400
bytes) and names the first vendor return code. The [強制關閉] level rule is unchanged.
tests/test_mainclose_stop.cpp [20]: the 19:11 case closes; servo ON / PTP / HOMING / velocity / invalid-read cases still hold;
T1-T19 unchanged. ctest MainCloseStop passes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
